<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cobbold Commission</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1962</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Cobbold Commission was a commission of enquiry set up by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malaya">Malaya</a> in 1962, chaired by Lord Cobbold, to find out whether the peoples of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sabah">North Borneo</a> and Sarawak supported joining the proposed Federation of Malaysia. It found about two-thirds in favour, subject to safeguards, and Malaysia was formed on 16 September 1963.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cobbold-commission.jpg" alt="Cobbold Commission" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MapGrid (old version SKopp, Zscout370 and Ranking Update) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Malaysia.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
